# File: tests/features/add_greeting_sha256_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/206-add-greeting-sha256-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Fingerprint the completed greeting with SHA-256

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Return the SHA-256 hex digest of the completed greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_sha256 is called with Ada
    Then the result is the Python str 7da4681c4837bb56185adc6967f0c6847c33148afb0ba4aefac709465da75f66
    And it is the SHA-256 digest of the 10 UTF-8 bytes of Hello, Ada written as 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Hash the exact UTF-8 code points without normalization
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_sha256 is called with Zo followed by precomposed U+00EB and with Zoe followed by combining U+0308
    Then the results are aadd4ee82814c54de89ac9cd0e8f089a485196e4952ee920db669caccb7c2524 and af1a0a3bab8dec9c18ed0501706ead61457c718667ae4bcfd5a7dbd525192064

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_sha256 is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper without changing existing surfaces
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_sha256 of Ada, and nmg-smoke Ada runs
    Then the example prints 7da4681c4837bb56185adc6967f0c6847c33148afb0ba4aefac709465da75f66
    And greeting_sha256 is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__ alongside every previously listed export
    And nmg-smoke prints Hello, Ada with one newline and exit status 0
    And the README documents the 64-character lowercase hex format, UTF-8 encoding of the complete greeting, absence of Unicode normalization, and the inherited invalid-name error
